Incorporated / derived work
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

moes_dimmer_3_gang uses a shared Tuya EF00 datapoint base (generic
cluster/device classes for talking to Tuya's manufacturer-specific cluster)
derived from:

- JohanBendz/com.tuya.zigbee — MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020-2024 Johan Bendz
  https://github.com/JohanBendz/com.tuya.zigbee

Johan Bendz's project does not include a 3-gang Moes dimmer driver (his
closest equivalent is 2-gang); the datapoint map, per-gang sub-device logic,
fan-speed handling, debounce/motor-protection logic, and settings for this
specific device were written independently, based on sniffer captures of the
actual hardware (_TZE204_1v1dxkck / TS0601).

moes_radar_sensor_mmwave (Linptech mmWave presence sensor, TS0225) is
original work with no third-party code: reverse-engineered from scratch via
Zigbee sniffer captures (CC2531 + Wireshark) and protocol analysis on
hardware owned by the author.
